      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The equation $(x - 5)^2 = 9$ can be written as $(x - 5) - 3 = 0$ by using the square root function. Thus, one root of the equation is $x = 8$. Similarly, another root is $x = 2$ by using the square root function on both sides of the equation. Therefore, the sum of the roots is $$(x = 8) + (x = 2) = 10.$$ The sum of the roots of the equation $$(x - 5)^2 = 9$$ is 10.",
